priorities_preventing_gambling_harm:
>Bradford Gambling Harm Prevention Working Group are to focus on

Strengthen the evidence base: A) Conduct a Health Needs Assessment (HNA) to understand the burden and distribution of GRH in your area. B) Reach out and explore opportunities to collaborate with academics and research groups who are studying GRH and the commercial determinants of health;

>Building leadership and capacity: C) Use and promote the Good Governance Toolkit to support decision making across the whole local authority;

>Reduce exposure and access: D) developing a local profile which includes public health evidence. This will underpin your Statement of Licensing Policy and brings data and evidence together to inform decision-making around licensing and planning alike. E) Raise awareness among support staff and local operators that support individuals with conditions such as learning disability, neurodevelopmental disorders, severe and enduring mental illness, Parkinson’s disease or dementia, lack of capacity to understand risk of gambling products or have increased susceptibility of harm

>Life course and equity approach: F) Work with treatment services to ensure they are equitable, provided according to need and are acceptable and accessible to those who require them, to reduce inequalities. Co-design of these services and pathways is a way to achieve this. G) Work with social care to ensure pathways are in place and appropriate action can be taken on an individual bases where vulnerabilities are present. H) Develop, offer and promote evidence-based training on gambling harms (including gaming) to frontline staff working in CYP settings – including head teachers – about the risk of GRH, actions to take

>Provide treatment and support for those affected by gambling harms:        I) Raise awareness of and signpost individuals to industry-independent resources and support services on gambling harms. J) Signpost treatment and support options visibly in your local area. K) Provide clear options for self-exclusion.
